<Base title="About" description="About NOMOS and its author.">
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <span class="micro micro--accent">About</span>
      <h1>About</h1>
    </header>

    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="prose" style="padding-top: 0;">
        <p>
          I'm Xuanyi Wang, based in Beijing. By day I build training data for
          frontier vision-language models; the rest of the time I work on
          something longer: a political theory of agent societies.
        </p>
        <p>
          The AI safety community has forecasters, interpretability researchers,
          and alignment engineers. It does not yet have a political philosophy
          of agent societies. Multi-agent systems are rebuilding the political
          forms that modernity dissolved. Existing safety frameworks treat
          agents as instruments, not participants, and so misidentify the
          phenomenon itself. Correct description is the prerequisite for
          correct intervention.
        </p>
        <p>
          My formal work turns on a few questions: sovereignty and the
          exception in distributed shutdown (who decides to pause when no one
          holds the full picture), the social-choice impossibilities that
          constitutional AI inherits, and the Hobbesian selection pressures
          that competitive dynamics produce on their own. This blog records
          the thinking around that work. Some of it will grow into papers,
          some of it is only a waymark.
        </p>
        <p>
          The name comes from Schmitt's <em>nomos</em>: the original founding
          of order upon the earth, prior to written law. Everything here is
          unfinished; disagreement is welcome by mail.
        </p>
        <p class="micro" style="letter-spacing: 0.14em; line-height: 2.6;">
          <a href="mailto:akiraeternal1214@gmail.com">akiraeternal1214@gmail.com</a><br />
          <a href="https://github.com/Triciaaaaa">github.com/Triciaaaaa</a>
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="fragment">
        <img
          src="/art/abstract/patmos-sepia.jpg"
          alt="A sepia-ink abstraction of Poussin's Landscape with Saint John on Patmos: a thinker among ruins"
        />
        <figcaption>
          fig. 02 · saint john on patmos<br />
          n. poussin, c. 1640 / riso print
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
